{
  "format": 2,
  "kind": "session",
  "name": "History availability boundaries",
  "description": "The effective lower bound (history_log_id, or latest_log_id + 1 when null, using the frame's or page's own head) is inclusive and only grows. When it grows the client evicts the room's messages whose latest snapshot is below it; if it overtakes the next position a recovery needs (reported by a room frame or a page) the client rebuilds from the new bound with the same H, keeping buffered live records at or above the bound. Continuation arithmetic is numeric on sparse millisecond IDs. A null bound needs no request until a later room frame reports a head above the checkpoint. The fixture server clamps pages to 2 records. Each variant ends with its own expectation.",
  "references": [
    "PROTOCOL.md#34-rooms",
    "PROTOCOL.md#appendix-a--history"
  ],
  "variants": [
